+## 4a. Corollary 5 — A3 is not needed for the aggregate conclusions
+
+*Derived by ChatGPT; independently checked by Claude.* Assume (A1)–(A2) only, and let the decomposition contain all pair curves.
+
+Put M := Σ_i N_{pair i} and G(t,t′) := Σ_i h(v_i,v_i) t_i t̄′_i. G is positive definite on K^m, hence on L.
+
+Proposition 3 gives S(x, My) = −G(τx, τy). The argument:
+1. If My = 0, then G(τx, τy) = 0 for all x. Since τ is surjective, τy = 0. Conversely, τy = 0 gives My = 0 by Lemma 2. So ker M = ker τ.
+2. Then rank M = 2(m−n) − (m−n) = m − n.
+3. im M ⊆ Σ_i im N_{pair i} ⊆ ker τ. Comparing dimensions, both inclusions are equalities.
+
+Hence Σ_e im N_e = ker τ = I without (A3). (H0), (H1), (H3) and (H4) never used (A3). The only role of (A3) is to make each single pair operator N_{pair i} nonzero.
+
+ChatGPT also checked a supplementary exact example in which (A3) fails: V = K², roots (1,0), (1,1), (1,1), dihedral image of order 8. Claude replayed it.
